---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
const title = 'Zodiacs AI Integration Candidates | Zodiacs.org';
const description = 'Review the public-sky ChatGPT app and local developer plugin candidates, their supported tools, privacy and installation requirements.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/developers/ai/">
  <section class="section container container--narrow ai-page">
    <em class="kicker">Developer tools · Review candidate</em>
    <h1 class="display">Build with the sky</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Two integration candidates connect assistants to the published Zodiacs engine: a public-sky ChatGPT app and a local developer plugin. Both use engine 0.1.1-rc.16. Local marketplace installation and bounded host testing are recorded; public listings and production activation remain release gates.</p>
      <h2>Sky questions and fact checks</h2>
      <p>The ChatGPT candidate computes positions at an explicit instant, finds sign ingresses, stations and new/full Moons in a window of up to 31 days, and checks astronomical claims. Answers include UTC, a display timezone, calculation receipts and numerical limits. A date-only claim can return <code>depends</code>. Event-search completeness is tested, not proven.</p>
      <p>Its sky calendar declares sidebar and conversation-panel entrypoints. Opening the calendar shows the next seven days in UTC. Date controls use midnight UTC; a display timezone changes the event labels. The initial result appears without another calculation request. These host entrypoints have been exercised in ChatGPT staging.</p>
      <p>Ask “What changes this week in Bangkok?” or “Did the Sun enter Libra on September 23, 2026?” An answer should be useful in the conversation. Links to the <a href="/moon-phase/">Moon tool</a>, <a href="/full-moon-calendar/">lunar calendar</a> and <a href="/developers/compute/">calculation method</a> offer optional further exploration.</p>
      <p>The hosted endpoint is disabled by default in the candidate. Public release and production activation remain release gates. It offers no birth-chart storage, scheduling, eclipse search or predictions of personal outcomes.</p>
      <h2>Build and verify an integration</h2>
      <p>Zodiacs Developer provides skills for building with the engine, checking output and testing an integration. Its local stdio server adds natal-chart calculation and record comparison to the public-sky tools. It opens no listener or outbound connection. The <a href="/developers/mcp/">existing local MCP adapter</a> remains available separately.</p>
      <p>In a checkout, run <code>npm ci</code> and <code>npm test</code> in <code>plugins/zodiacs-developer</code>. The candidate contains pinned dependencies, three skills and runnable synthetic sky/calendar examples. Installation details and review evidence are in the <a href="https://github.com/zodiacs-org/site/tree/main/plugins/zodiacs-developer">plugin directory</a>; that repository link will contain this candidate after its changes are published.</p>
      <h2>What local means</h2>
      <p>The developer server computes on its machine. The assistant provider can still receive the arguments and results. Hosted sky calculations run on Zodiacs infrastructure. Public-sky tools need no birth details; derived natal positions remain personal data. Read the <a href="/privacy/#ai-integrations">AI integration privacy explanation</a> before connecting personal records.</p>
      <p>Use the published <a href="/developers/engine/">calculation engine</a> in external projects and preserve its notices. Site-derived candidate code retains the site's license. A receipt supports reproduction; it does not certify an imported record's authenticity or validate astrological interpretation.</p>
      <p>For current support and known calculation limitations, see <a href="/developers/support/">developer support</a> and <a href="/developers/conformance/">independent-reference conformance</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  .ai-page h1 { margin: var(--s-3) 0 var(--s-6); }
  .ai-page h2 { margin-top: var(--s-10); font-size: var(--text-lg); }
  .ai-page code { font-family: var(--font-mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
</style>
